          "summary": "Default deliverables to Customer-owned Type I Materials, broaden the Type II licence-back, and confirm Customer ownership of Content/data",
          "comment": "[Playbook] We own the work product we pay for, so we have made Type I (Customer-owned) the default for Materials created during the Services and broadened the Type II licence to let us modify and sublicense IBM's pre-existing materials embedded in deliverables. We have also confirmed that we retain all rights in our Content and data, which the Agreement currently leaves unstated.",
          "precedentId": "seed-ip",
          "ops": [
            {
              "kind": "replace",
              "paragraphId": "p0082",
              "oldText": "If not specified, Materials will be considered Type II Materials.",
              "newText": "If not specified, Materials created during the Service performance period will be considered Type I Materials."
            },
            {
              "kind": "replace",
              "paragraphId": "p0085",
              "oldText": "IBM grants Customer an irrevocable, nonexclusive, worldwide, paid-up license to use, execute, reproduce, display, perform, and distribute, within Customer's Enterprise only, copies of Type II Materials.",
              "newText": "IBM grants Customer a perpetual, irrevocable, nonexclusive, worldwide, paid-up license to use, execute, reproduce, display, perform, distribute, modify and prepare derivative works based on, and sublicense, copies of Type II Materials for Customer's business purposes."
            },
            {
              "kind": "insert_after",
              "paragraphId": "p0086",
              "numbering": "e.",
              "text": "Customer retains all right, title, and interest (including ownership of copyright and all other intellectual property rights) in and to the Content and the Customer Components, including all data Customer or its Services Recipients provide or process through the e-business Hosting Environment, and nothing in this Agreement assigns or transfers any such rights to IBM."
            }
          ]
        },
